/* book Worked example: Q: Profile levelling was done along the centre line of a proposed road from a BM of RL 85.250 m. The readings were: BS 1.420 on the BM; IS 1.865 at chainage 0, 2.310 at 20 m and 2.945 at 40 m; FS 3.280 at 60 m (change point); BS 0.865 at 60 m; IS 1.540 at 80 m and 2.105 at 100 m; FS 2.660 at 120 m. The formation starts at RL 84.200 m at chainage 0 and falls at 1 in 50. Find the ground RLs, the depth of cutting or filling at each peg, and where the formation meets the ground.
   1. Set-up 1: HI = 85.250 + 1.420 = 86.670 m. RLs: ch 0 = 86.670 − 1.865 = 84.805; ch 20 = 84.360; ch 40 = 83.725; ch 60 (FS) = 86.670 − 3.280 = 83.390 m.
   2. Set-up 2: HI = 83.390 + 0.865 = 84.255 m. RLs: ch 80 = 84.255 − 1.540 = 82.715; ch 100 = 82.150; ch 120 (FS) = 84.255 − 2.660 = 81.595 m.
   3. Arithmetic check: ΣBS − ΣFS = (1.420 + 0.865) − (3.280 + 2.660) = 2.285 − 5.940 = −3.655 m; last RL − first RL = 81.595 − 85.250 = −3.655 m. It agrees.
   4. Formation falls 1 in 50, that is 0.400 m per 20 m: 84.200, 83.800, 83.400, 83.000, 82.600, 82.200 and 81.800 m at chainages 0 to 120.
   5. Ground − formation at each peg: ch 0: 84.805 − 84.200 = 0.605 m cut; ch 20: 0.560 m cut; ch 40: 0.325 m cut; ch 60: 0.390 m cut; ch 80: 0.115 m cut; ch 100: 82.150 − 82.200 = −0.050 m, so 0.050 m fill; ch 120: 81.595 − 81.800 = −0.205 m, so 0.205 m fill.
   6. The cut changes to fill between 80 m (cut 0.115 m) and 100 m (fill 0.050 m). Assuming straight ground between pegs, the formation meets the ground at 80 + 20 × 0.115 ÷ (0.115 + 0.050) = 80 + 13.94 = 93.94 m.
   Answer: Ground RLs from 84.805 m at chainage 0 to 81.595 m at 120 m; cutting from 0.605 m down to 0.115 m up to 80 m, filling of 0.050 m and 0.205 m at 100 m and 120 m; the cut-fill (zero) point is at chainage 93.94 m. */
