/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Each line of the level book is one staff station.
   - Check 1 tests only the BS, FS and change-point arithmetic.
   - Within one set-up the line of sight is fixed, so a smaller reading means the staff stands on higher ground.
   - Rise and fall are booked as positive numbers in their own columns; the heading carries the sign.
   - Every IS enters a rise or a fall, so this one three-way check tests all the arithmetic.
   - The page of the first worked example, both methods in one table (in an exam use the columns asked for):
*/
