/* book Worked example: Q: The following readings were taken with a level and a 4 m staff on ground falling towards a stream crossed by a bridge: 1.235 (BM, RL 100.000 m), 1.870 (P1), 2.645 (P2), 3.410 and 0.580 (change point CP1), −1.725 (staff inverted under the bridge soffit S), 1.465 (P3, on the bank below S), 2.950 and 1.105 (change point CP2), 2.230 (P4), 2.865 (TBM). Book and reduce the levels by the height of collimation method and by the rise and fall method, apply all the checks, and find the clear height of the soffit above P3.
   1. Set-up 1: HI = 100.000 + 1.235 = 101.235 m. P1 = 101.235 − 1.870 = 99.365; P2 = 101.235 − 2.645 = 98.590; CP1 = 101.235 − 3.410 = 97.825 m.
   2. Set-up 2: HI = 97.825 + 0.580 = 98.405 m. Soffit S = 98.405 − (−1.725) = 100.130 m; P3 = 98.405 − 1.465 = 96.940; CP2 = 98.405 − 2.950 = 95.455 m.
   3. Set-up 3: HI = 95.455 + 1.105 = 96.560 m. P4 = 96.560 − 2.230 = 94.330; TBM = 96.560 − 2.865 = 93.695 m.
   4. Rise and fall: 1.235 → 1.870 fall 0.635; 1.870 → 2.645 fall 0.775; 2.645 → 3.410 fall 0.765; 0.580 → −1.725 rise 2.305; −1.725 → 1.465 fall 3.190; 1.465 → 2.950 fall 1.485; 1.105 → 2.230 fall 1.125; 2.230 → 2.865 fall 0.635. Adding these to 100.000 m gives the same RLs.
   5. Check 1: ΣBS − ΣFS = 2.920 − 9.225 = −6.305 = ΣRise − ΣFall = 2.305 − 8.610 = −6.305 = last RL − first RL = 93.695 − 100.000 = −6.305 m.
   6. Full HI check: Σ(HI × n) = 101.235 × 3 + 98.405 × 3 + 96.560 × 2 = 792.040; minus ΣIS (6.485, the inverted reading counted as −1.725) and ΣFS (9.225) gives 776.330 m, which equals the sum of the eight RLs after the BM, 776.330 m.
   7. Clear height of soffit above P3 = 100.130 − 96.940 = 3.190 m (the fall from S to P3).
   Answer: RLs: P1 99.365, P2 98.590, CP1 97.825, soffit 100.130, P3 96.940, CP2 95.455, P4 94.330, TBM 93.695 m. All checks give −6.305 m and the full HI check balances at 776.330 m. The soffit is 3.190 m above P3. */
