/* book Worked example 2: Q: Complete the following page of a level book (rise and fall method) and apply the check. Station 1: BS 2.215, RL 150.000 (BM). Station 2: IS 1.680. Station 3: BS 1.950, FS missing, fall 1.210. Station 4: IS missing, rise 0.640. Station 5: IS 0.775. Station 6: BS missing, FS 1.435. Station 7: FS 2.310, RL 148.390.
   1. Station 2: rise = 2.215 − 1.680 = 0.535; RL = 150.535 m.
   2. Station 3: fall 1.210 = FS − 1.680, so FS = 2.890; RL = 150.535 − 1.210 = 149.325 m.
   3. Station 4: rise 0.640 = 1.950 − IS, so IS = 1.310; RL = 149.325 + 0.640 = 149.965 m.
   4. Station 5: rise = 1.310 − 0.775 = 0.535; RL = 150.500 m.
   5. Station 6: fall = 1.435 − 0.775 = 0.660; RL = 149.840 m.
   6. Station 7: fall = 149.840 − 148.390 = 1.450 = 2.310 − BS(6), so the missing BS at station 6 = 0.860 m.
   7. Check: ΣBS = 2.215 + 1.950 + 0.860 = 5.025; ΣFS = 2.890 + 1.435 + 2.310 = 6.635; ΣBS − ΣFS = −1.610. ΣRise = 1.710, ΣFall = 3.320, difference −1.610. Last − first = 148.390 − 150.000 = −1.610 m.
   Answer: Missing entries: FS at 3 = 2.890, IS at 4 = 1.310, BS at 6 = 0.860; RLs 150.535, 149.325, 149.965, 150.500, 149.840 m; all three check values are −1.610 m. */
